{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:9d27b12029ae3f0d","name":"The Commerce Guild","source":{"id":"source:reference-9d27b12029ae3f0d","title":"The Commerce Guild","revision":23766,"timestamp":"2024-10-06T21:38:28Z","sha256":"328c4f5a964cb41a2566bdecb1b82843e416402fa61140ea4d4e1ac99c7d5cc5","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=23766","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=The%20Commerce%20Guild&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-9d27b12029ae3f0d","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Clone Wars Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Clone_Wars_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Commerce Guild comes to ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Confederacy of Independent Systems"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Confederacy_of_Independent_Systems","referenceId":"reference:dfc46c9d666b9b41"}," in secret. As the most influential commodities broker in ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Republic","referenceId":"reference:332055cafc4223eb"},", it knows all too well that too much pressure here or there can severely unbalance the market, costing hundreds of trillions of credits. But after a few of the more cagey prospective members of the Confederacy die in convenient accidents, Commerce Guild President ",{"tag":"a","children":["Shu Mai"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Shu_Mai?action=edit&redlink=1"},"- a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gossam"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gossam?action=edit&redlink=1"},", from the world of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Castell"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Castell?action=edit&redlink=1"},"- decides that she can play both sides of the conflict without arousing the ire of either; both the Republic and the Confederacy need ore and minerals and bulk produce, particularly in wartime.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Commerce Guild employs a force of security personnel and Battle Droids whose major function is to keep The Commerce Guild's member worlds and systems in line. The organic personnel generally work separately from the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"},", though most of the Commerce Guild's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid"}," forces are commanded and maintained by ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gossams"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gossams?action=edit&redlink=1"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Command Structure"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The command structure of The Commerce Guild's organic forces follows a similar command structure to the Republic's special forces.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Squad (6 Officers):"]}," A Squad consists of six ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gossam"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gossam?action=edit&redlink=1"}," security officers (usually Gossam Commandos), one of whom acts as a Squad Leader."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Troop (36 Officers):"]}," A Troop consists of six Squads, including six Squad Leaders. They are generally led by a single ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gossam"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gossam?action=edit&redlink=1"}," with the title of Security Chief."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Division (216 Officers plus support personnel):"]}," A Company consists of 6 Troops, led by six Security Chiefs and a Division Commander."]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The Commerce Guild's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid"}," forces are arranged by type of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid"},". \n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Advanced DSD Unit:"]}," This Unit consists of one ",{"tag":"a","children":["Advanced Dwarf Spider Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Advanced_Dwarf_Spider_Droid","referenceId":"reference:8f5c0adc64fdf8fe"}," and a support group of one Squad of ",{"tag":"a","children":["B1-Series Battle Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/B1-Series_Battle_Droids"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["B2-Series Super Battle Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/B2-Series_Super_Battle_Droids"},"."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Spelunker Probe Droid Unit:"]}," This unit includes five ",{"tag":"a","children":["Spelunker Probe Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Spelunker_Probe_Droids"},". Forces of up to 20 Units are sometimes fielded to handle particularly tough targets."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Dwarf Spider Droid Unit:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dwarf Spider Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dwarf_Spider_Droids"}," usually operate in groups of four, or in forces of 2-5 Units."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Heavy Dwarf Spider Droid Unit:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Advanced Dwarf Spider Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Advanced_Dwarf_Spider_Droids"}," usually operate in groups of four, or in forces of 2-5 Units."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["OG-9 Homing Spider Droid Unit:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["OG-9 Homing Spider Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/OG-9_Homing_Spider_Droids"}," are almost always fielded singly, though usually with an escort of four ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dwarf Spider Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dwarf_Spider_Droids"}," (which also act as spotters)."]}]},"\n","\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
